<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Complexity Analysis</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> be the prediction horizon, <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> the number of forecast segments, <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> the segment length, and <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> the hidden dimension.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Autoregressive decoding.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">AR models generate one step at a time, yielding a total complexity of</p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\text{AR}}=\mathcal{O}(K\cdot d^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mtext>AR</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\text{AR}}=\mathcal{O}(K\cdot d^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which scales linearly with <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and limits parallelism.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Non-autoregressive decoding.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">KAIROS predicts <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S{=}K/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S{=}K/L</annotation></semantics></math> segments in parallel, each via a mixture-of-experts head:</p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\text{NAR}}=\mathcal{O}(S\cdot d^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mtext>NAR</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\text{NAR}}=\mathcal{O}(S\cdot d^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus the cost depends on <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> rather than <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, and all segments can be generated in a single forward pass.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Parallelism.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This design makes inference nearly independent of horizon length, enabling substantial speedup over AR decoding while retaining segment-level modeling flexibility.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Formalization of Multi-Peak Distribution</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In forecasting, the conditional distribution of future <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> given history <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is often <em id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multi-peak</em>:</p>
<table id="A4.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{Y}\mid\mathbf{X})=\sum_{m=1}^{M}\pi_{m}(\mathbf{X})\,p_{m}(\mathbf{Y}\mid\mathbf{X})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{Y}\mid\mathbf{X})=\sum_{m=1}^{M}\pi_{m}(\mathbf{X})\,p_{m}(\mathbf{Y}\mid\mathbf{X}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where different modes <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to distinct but plausible futures.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Conventional NAR models trained with pointwise losses approximate the expectation</p>
<table id="A4.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{Y}}\approx\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{Y}\mid\mathbf{X})}[\mathbf{Y}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{Y}}\approx\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{Y}\mid\mathbf{X})}[\mathbf{Y}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">leading to over-smoothed predictions. This motivates segment-wise expert modeling to preserve diverse futures.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>. </span><span id="A4.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Detailed dataset descriptions. Dataset sizes are listed as (Train, Validation, Test).</span></figcaption>
<table id="A4.T6.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T6.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Tasks</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Dataset</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Dim</span></th>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Series Length</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Dataset Size</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Frequency</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Forecastability<math id="A4.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ast" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ast</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.5.1.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Information</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"></th>
<th id="A4.T6.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T6.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">ETTm1</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T6.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">7</span></th>
<td id="A4.T6.5.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T6.5.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">{96, 192, 336, 720}</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.5.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T6.5.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(34465, 11521, 11521)</span></td>
